 "through_line": "Udaypur's inscriptions as evidence of literate royal culture: the signed six lines of 1080; the faulty V.S. 1116 inscription kept apart (held, RR-1); Amērā's dated verse; the praśasti as object, self-portrait, genealogy and claimed conquests, and its lost maker; the serpent of letters and its fellows, Dhārā's halls, Bhoja's books and the courts' poets; the dating of letters; the porch archive under Caulukya then Paramāra masters; the last Paramāra traces; Persian from 1336; the hill's pilgrims and unread lines; the limits of the record, into Chapter 7.",
